WEBVTT

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:07.600
Not enough...

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:10.460
It is no match...

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:13.360
All of it... everything!

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.570
But I will overcome this...

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.310
Though my body may crumble to dust!

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:23.300
This craving, this thirst... 
I cannot escape it!

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:27.240
I will carry this desire through! I will 
submit to the demands of my blood!

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.520
I will be faithful to this hunger!

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:38.640
<b>Daedalus</b>

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:45.100
This is great!

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:50.140
Both now and long ago,
the kids are just so much fun...

00:01:10.790 --> 00:01:14.010
<b>Is It Wrong to Try to Pick Up Girls in a Dungeon? III</b>

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:24.160
Knossos
Man-Made Labyrinth

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:24.190
Where have you taken our kin?

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:25.900
Tell me, human!

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:29.400
I've told you, I-I don't know...

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:30.880
Don't play innocent!

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:33.320
You lowlifes reek of it...

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:36.270
The scent of Ranieh's poison!

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:40.340
Answer the question! Where are our kin?

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:46.270
The eastern edge... There's a door...

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:47.480
A door?

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:53.990
It's not like you'll able to get in, anyway.

00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:59.290
You guys... don't have it...

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.410
Commander Shakti! Ilta-san! Over there!

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:08.370
Armed monsters!

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:10.840
Great work, Nantoka!

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:14.330
My name is Modaka! 
Please, remember it already!

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:17.240
I know, I know, Kantoka.

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:21.030
I'm telling you, it's Modaka! You have 
no intention of remembering, do you?

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:25.120
That bearing is due east.

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:26.760
The deep forest?

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:28.390
Why would they go there?

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:30.820
What do you want to do?

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:32.890
We will divide the corps in two.

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:36.530
Momonga! Head to Livira and check 
to see if there are any survivors.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:37.670
Yes, Commander!

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:40.720
The rest of you, follow me! We head east!

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:40.690
Also, my name is Modaka!

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:51.700
The suppression force's 
objective is to tame them!

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:53.250
Do not kill! Bring them in alive!

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:54.550
Go on ahead!

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:55.840
Lett!

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:10.730
That lot from the Ganesha Familia 
seem to be getting pushed back.

00:04:10.730 --> 00:04:13.930
Those armed monsters... are strong.

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:17.500
We are only here to gather information 
and to look out for Bell Cranel.

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:18.820
I will go and assist.

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:20.320
Wha—Lion?

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:23.050
We've lost sight of Cranel-san.

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:25.320
I will look as I fight.

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:28.220
You're quite overprotective, 
too, aren't you?

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:31.450
Wait, both of you! At least stay invisible!

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:33.290
Oh, honestly!

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:40.800
Lyd-san!

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:44.080
Why have you come here, Bell-cchi?

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:55.360
Wha—Antianeira?

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:57.020
Why are you here?

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:00.040
Don't worry about the details.

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:02.990
You're shorthanded, aren't you?

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:10.160
Wh-Who are you?

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:12.870
Just a passing stranger.

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:17.840
Why... Why have you come, Bell-cchi?

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:24.470
I heard that Livira... had been 
destroyed by armed monsters...

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:27.840
Lyd-san, was it really you 
and the others who did that?

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:32.000
Yes. It was us who attacked.

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:33.270
Why?

00:05:35.590 --> 00:05:38.980
Our kin were killed... by poachers.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:44.660
Wiene and others were taken by their group.

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:45.650
Wiene was?

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:48.190
I'm sorry, Bell-cchi...

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:52.630
We really are monsters, 
just like humans say we are.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:53.740
What?

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:56.820
I tried to talk... to convince them!

00:05:56.820 --> 00:05:58.210
But it wasn't any good!

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:02.180
I'm the same! I can't suppress my rage!

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:04.940
The ones who killed my kin...

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:06.840
I want to kill them so much I can't help it!

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:10.700
We will go save Wiene and the others.

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:13.230
We will bring back our kin!

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:14.690
Lyd-san...

00:06:15.550 --> 00:06:16.300
I'll go, too...

00:06:16.300 --> 00:06:16.980
Stay back!

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:20.600
Bell-cchi, you're a human, right?

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:23.540
Stop caring about monsters. Turn back!

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:24.630
Lyd-san!

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:29.000
If you're seen with us, 
that'll be the end for you, Bell-cchi!

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:30.970
What're you dragging your heels for?

00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:32.860
Hurry up and go back to 
Lili-cchi and the others!

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:34.080
Lyd-san...

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:35.290
Go!

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:36.490
Lyd-san!

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:37.940
Go away!

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:40.180
Even so, I...

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:42.960
Cranel-san!

00:06:52.570 --> 00:06:54.770
Are you unharmed, Cranel-san?

00:06:54.770 --> 00:06:56.640
Ryu-san... Why...

00:06:57.010 --> 00:07:00.790
I will tell you of the details later. 
It is dangerous to remain isolated.

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:03.270
Let us return to the Ganesha Familia.

00:07:05.850 --> 00:07:07.060
Cranel-san?

00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:10.060
I'm sorry, Ryu-san...

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:13.280
I'm going after that monster.

00:07:13.690 --> 00:07:14.910
I have to go after him!

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:20.850
This incident involves the dark faction...

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:24.930
A familia with some kind of connection 
to Evilus is involved.

00:07:24.930 --> 00:07:26.330
That is what I have heard.

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:31.840
I cannot tolerate the existence of Evilus.

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:35.840
I do not want you to be the least bit 
involved with something like that.

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:40.630
Won't you return to the surface?

00:07:41.110 --> 00:07:42.680
Syr will be worried.

00:07:46.990 --> 00:07:48.380
I see.

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:51.830
You have ended up becoming an 
adventurer through and through.

00:07:54.090 --> 00:07:55.940
I'm certain there is no point 
in trying to stop you.

00:07:56.940 --> 00:07:57.950
Take this.

00:07:58.330 --> 00:07:59.960
If you find yourself in trouble, use it.

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:09.640
I don't know if it will prove useful, but...

00:08:10.100 --> 00:08:11.790
Thank you.

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:12.750
Ryu-san...

00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:16.120
I'm sorry!

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:22.460
Gros!

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:23.530
Have you found the door?

00:08:23.990 --> 00:08:25.740
No good! I can't find it!

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:29.180
Even when I call for our kin,
there is no answer!

00:08:30.070 --> 00:08:32.570
Gran, go open the door.

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:35.040
You sure, Dix?

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:40.460
We should invite them in, 
don't you think? Those monsters.

00:08:41.690 --> 00:08:44.130
We'll finish the hunt here.

00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:51.000
Bell Cranel!

00:08:53.390 --> 00:08:54.390
Fels-san!

00:08:54.980 --> 00:08:58.650
I am glad to have met up with you. 
Gros and the others have headed east.

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:05.130
It seems they caught poachers in town 
and acquired the information from them,

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:08.110
that there is a door on the eastern edge.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:11.910
There's no one here...

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:15.070
This is the edge of the floor.

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:17.280
There is no other "eastern edge."

00:09:21.230 --> 00:09:23.150
Bell Cranel, what is that?

00:09:25.650 --> 00:09:27.700
It seems to be reacting to something.

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:29.270
It couldn't be...

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:34.050
Stand back, Bell Cranel.

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:53.860
This is not like the Dungeon.

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:56.890
It is clearly man-made.

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:04.370
Is this...

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:07.820
Orichalcum!

00:10:08.390 --> 00:10:11.750
It is the strongest refined metal,
 surpassing adamantite.

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:16.870
If this is true, then even with magic, 
it is impossible to destroy it, but...

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:29.350
I cannot believe it.

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:31.950
To think something like this 
existed in the Dungeon...

00:10:38.110 --> 00:10:41.070
<b>Daedalus</b>

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:40.700
Daedalus?

00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:47.520
Damn it! So all we can do is wait?

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:52.210
With it under such tight control, 
even sneaking in isn't a possibility.

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:55.410
Just waiting is really tough, isn't it?

00:10:55.410 --> 00:10:58.590
It's always like this for me, Welf-kun.

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:00.120
Huh? Oh. Right...

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:01.170
Bell-sama...

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:06.000
Hey, if this incident was 
caused by poachers,

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:07.880
then couldn't we try to find their hideout?

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:10.910
If they're selling off the 
Xenos aboveground,

00:11:10.910 --> 00:11:13.310
then they must have a base in 
Orario somewhere, right?

00:11:13.310 --> 00:11:15.860
True. That is certainly a possibility.

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:19.220
But how would we find them?

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:27.770
Deciding on a monetary value for 
monsters and selling them off...

00:11:28.280 --> 00:11:32.260
We're talking about a familia that doesn't 
fear the Dungeon, let alone gods...

00:11:32.260 --> 00:11:35.150
They won't be easy to find...

00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:38.890
A monetary value for monsters?

00:11:42.810 --> 00:11:45.680
To think you would ever come here...

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:47.200
Arde...

00:11:48.420 --> 00:11:50.590
I have a question for you...

00:11:51.190 --> 00:11:53.220
regarding "talking monsters."

00:11:54.260 --> 00:11:57.690
You have that rare transformation magic.

00:11:58.180 --> 00:12:03.550
Back then, you lured monsters out, 
captured them, and sold them.

00:12:03.550 --> 00:12:04.910
That's what you said, right?

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:08.900
Back then, I thought it was 
ridiculous and just ignored it.

00:12:09.300 --> 00:12:12.360
I didn't think there was any way to 
assign a monetary value to monsters.

00:12:13.070 --> 00:12:15.710
But... it's different now.

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:17.870
I see.

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:21.580
Have you met them, Arde?

00:12:21.580 --> 00:12:23.920
Those talking monsters?

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:27.630
If at the time you were 
complicit with the poachers,

00:12:27.990 --> 00:12:31.350
then you might have some idea where 
their hideout could be, correct?

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:33.790
Well, now...

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:36.120
If you were to go to Daedalus Street...

00:12:36.380 --> 00:12:38.470
You might learn something.

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:42.300
This is connected to Daedalus Street?

00:12:42.300 --> 00:12:43.340
Yes.

00:12:43.340 --> 00:12:47.990
They transport the captured Xenos 
to the surface without our knowing,

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:50.070
and smuggle them out through Orario.

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:55.070
If this place is connected to the surface,
 then everything is consistent.

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:58.590
<b>Daedalus</b>

00:12:56.110 --> 00:12:58.590
And that sign...

00:12:58.990 --> 00:13:02.060
It is, like Babel and Daedalus Street...

00:13:02.060 --> 00:13:05.900
structures which form the cornerstones 
of Orario, built by a master craftsman...

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:08.120
Built by Daedalus. 
There is no mistaking his work.

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:15.280
We have long considered the possibility of 
an entrance to the Dungeon other than Babel

00:13:15.280 --> 00:13:17.450
and investigated to that end, however.

00:13:18.760 --> 00:13:21.690
We have finally found it, Ouranos.

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:26.420
Ikelos...

00:13:26.420 --> 00:13:27.190
Yeah?

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:31.080
Looks like you found me, huh?

00:13:31.590 --> 00:13:34.450
You win at tag, Hermes.

00:13:35.470 --> 00:13:37.880
I can't stop this uproar,

00:13:37.880 --> 00:13:42.410
but as a reward for finding me, I will 
answer any question you like right now.

00:13:42.770 --> 00:13:45.620
So what would you like to ask?

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:49.500
The scent of our kin is close! Onward!

00:13:49.500 --> 00:13:52.760
Lyd! The door! This is a trap!

00:13:53.050 --> 00:13:54.220
I know.

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:56.190
But we have no choice but to go!

00:14:01.260 --> 00:14:02.470
What is this place?

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:08.370
Everyone!

00:14:09.670 --> 00:14:12.280
Break the cages! Free our kin!

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:19.510
Fear!

00:14:19.510 --> 00:14:20.470
Are you all right?

00:14:20.470 --> 00:14:21.790
What happened to Wiene?

00:14:22.690 --> 00:14:23.990
I don't know.

00:14:24.410 --> 00:14:27.120
They brought me here while 
I was unconscious.

00:14:28.630 --> 00:14:31.160
What a touching reunion!

00:14:31.590 --> 00:14:34.280
Good job making it here, monsters.

00:14:34.280 --> 00:14:36.010
Welcome.

00:14:36.010 --> 00:14:39.690
Are you the poacher who has 
been selling off our kin?

00:14:39.890 --> 00:14:42.010
Yes, I am.

00:14:42.010 --> 00:14:46.270
I had to hurt them quite a bit to make 
sure they wouldn't be rude to customers.

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:48.230
You evil...

00:14:48.520 --> 00:14:51.670
Well, to be perfectly accurate, it isn't "me."

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:54.160
It's "us," you see?

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:58.600
While protecting that 
precious baggage of yours...

00:14:58.600 --> 00:15:00.630
I wonder how well you'll be able to fight.

00:15:00.630 --> 00:15:01.710
Lyd-san!

00:15:02.820 --> 00:15:03.830
Bell-cchi?

00:15:03.830 --> 00:15:05.540
That boy from before!

00:15:05.540 --> 00:15:07.300
You little... Why have you come?

00:15:08.490 --> 00:15:09.970
Hey, Gran!

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:13.050
I don't remember telling 
you to invite a rabbit!

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:15.310
No, it wasn't...

00:15:15.590 --> 00:15:17.510
Dix! I know I did it right!

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:18.810
That's...

00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:22.600
A key?

00:15:24.050 --> 00:15:27.260
Oh... so that's what it is.

00:15:27.260 --> 00:15:30.420
For crying out loud. 
Which idiot let it get taken?

00:15:30.840 --> 00:15:33.570
Really not something I should go 
handing out everywhere, is it?

00:15:34.010 --> 00:15:36.980
Hazer. Dix Perdix.

00:15:36.980 --> 00:15:39.280
Are you the one behind this incident?

00:15:39.520 --> 00:15:42.300
And you, you're a mage, right?

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:44.180
Setting aside the Little Rookie,

00:15:44.180 --> 00:15:48.270
I'm wondering what connection 
you've got to the monsters, huh?

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:52.970
This man-made labyrinth is the 
work of Daedalus, is it not?

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:55.310
What are all of you doing in such a place?

00:15:57.160 --> 00:15:58.910
Doing? Nothing...

00:15:58.910 --> 00:16:02.260
This fine project has been forced 
on generation after generation.

00:16:02.740 --> 00:16:07.220
As I am a descendant, you've got no right 
to complain about what I do with it.

00:16:07.220 --> 00:16:09.940
Generations? Descendant?

00:16:09.940 --> 00:16:12.690
What, you don't believe me?

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:15.960
Fine. I'll show you.

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:19.560
This is what shows you're from 
the Daedalus family line...

00:16:19.560 --> 00:16:20.680
The proof!

00:16:22.230 --> 00:16:25.890
Every human who shares the 
blood of our scumbag ancestor

00:16:25.890 --> 00:16:28.870
is always born with these eyes!

00:16:28.870 --> 00:16:30.920
It's a blood binding!

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:33.870
A man-made labyrinth...

00:16:34.350 --> 00:16:38.400
and a blood binding passed down 
through Daedalus' descendants.

00:16:38.660 --> 00:16:43.520
You're saying Daedalus built a door 
that responds to those special eyes

00:16:44.110 --> 00:16:47.690
so that only his descendants would 
be able to continue his work.

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:53.030
Dix and the others gouged out the eyes 
of corpses and made them into keys.

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:54.900
I see.

00:16:55.460 --> 00:16:57.280
Thanks to you, I've started to understand...

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:00.290
the context of this incident.

00:17:02.070 --> 00:17:06.080
A thousand years ago, in the 
era when the gods descended...

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:09.800
When the Lower World was 
first blessed by the gods...

00:17:09.800 --> 00:17:13.720
When Ouranos brought Falna 
to his few followers...

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:16.230
Daedalus was there.

00:17:17.310 --> 00:17:19.290
After receiving Ouranos' divine intentions,

00:17:19.290 --> 00:17:21.430
he contributed to the 
construction of Orario.

00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:23.690
Having completed the construction of Babel,

00:17:23.690 --> 00:17:26.730
he was much praised by the gods.

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:30.570
He was truly... an unparalleled genius.

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:36.990
But even that genius took one look at the 
outrageous opus laid out at your feet,

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:39.120
and went completely insane!

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:42.790
The underground labyrinth... the Dungeon.

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:46.360
In his eyes, it exceeded human knowledge.

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:49.060
He saw it as an "opus."

00:17:50.530 --> 00:17:54.320
He was knocked out, overwhelmed!

00:17:54.320 --> 00:17:56.180
Broken! Haunted and obsessed!

00:17:56.580 --> 00:17:59.790
Once praised as an artisan, 
his words and deeds grew strange.

00:18:00.440 --> 00:18:01.870
He was labeled a freak.

00:18:01.870 --> 00:18:05.360
One day, he suddenly disappeared. 
Was that the reason for it?

00:18:05.360 --> 00:18:06.850
That's right!

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:08.770
An opus that would surpass the Dungeon.

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:10.810
He wanted to build it 
with his own two hands!

00:18:11.210 --> 00:18:14.510
It is the man-made labyrinth, Knossos!

00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:16.570
Knossos?

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:21.660
Daedalus' legacy... 
This, where we are now, is...

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:25.620
Well, it isn't finished, though.

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:28.880
The human limitation known as the lifespan...

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:34.490
Even a genius such as Daedalus 
couldn't win against old age.

00:18:35.400 --> 00:18:38.710
Even so, the guy just couldn't give up.

00:18:38.710 --> 00:18:43.340
He forced the partially completed Knossos 
and blueprints on his descendants...

00:18:43.800 --> 00:18:47.730
as a sort of kindhearted 
little bonus for them!

00:18:48.870 --> 00:18:50.380
Wait, Ikelos!

00:18:50.380 --> 00:18:52.450
If what you're saying is true, then...

00:18:52.450 --> 00:18:53.900
For a thousand years...

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:57.900
The descendants of Daedalus have 
continued to build this place!

00:18:58.400 --> 00:19:03.880
But after a thousand years, we've still 
only reached the Dungeon's middle levels.

00:19:05.770 --> 00:19:10.340
Takes too much, that creation of Daedalus.

00:19:10.770 --> 00:19:13.530
Too much time... and money.

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:18.270
Then the reason your Familia 
colluded with Evilus...

00:19:18.270 --> 00:19:21.390
It was all to complete Knossos?

00:19:22.270 --> 00:19:26.840
Then capturing Xenos and selling them 
was just one way of raising funds?

00:19:26.840 --> 00:19:29.860
Yeah. In the beginning, at least.

00:19:29.860 --> 00:19:31.740
That is enough tedious talk.

00:19:31.740 --> 00:19:36.990
You violated our kin! Killed Ranieh and 
the others! This does not change that!

00:19:36.990 --> 00:19:38.740
You will face the consequences!

00:19:43.860 --> 00:19:44.930
Lett!

00:19:51.280 --> 00:19:53.790
No reason to be stingy here.

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:55.250
Guess I'll use it right away.

00:19:56.210 --> 00:19:57.590
Get behind me!

00:19:58.170 --> 00:20:01.210
Lose your way in an unending illusion...

00:20:01.210 --> 00:20:03.830
Phobetor Daedalus!

00:20:20.880 --> 00:20:22.880
What's wrong with everyone?

00:20:22.880 --> 00:20:27.330
A curse. Unlike magic, 
a curse cannot be avoided.

00:20:27.750 --> 00:20:32.780
What he used is likely a curse which causes 
rampaging through bewitchment and confusion.

00:20:33.050 --> 00:20:34.360
But that can't...

00:20:34.360 --> 00:20:37.780
This robe defends against negative 
status effects and curses.

00:20:38.260 --> 00:20:40.840
There's some guys here it didn't work on.

00:20:42.180 --> 00:20:43.510
Not that it matters.

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:46.420
You can go get eaten by monsters!

00:20:58.840 --> 00:21:00.910
Forgive me, Lyd.

00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:05.350
Stop Hazer, Bell Cranel!

00:21:06.440 --> 00:21:09.760
This level of curse will be dispelled 
if the caster is brought down.

00:21:09.760 --> 00:21:11.730
Lyd and the others will 
return to their senses!

00:21:12.660 --> 00:21:15.060
You coming for me, Little Rookie?

00:21:15.060 --> 00:21:17.400
I'm Level 5, you know.

00:21:18.270 --> 00:21:21.170
A curse is powerful,
but casting one comes with collateral.

00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:25.000
That man must be paying some 
kind of price right now!

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:26.630
Damn it.

00:21:26.950 --> 00:21:28.350
Don't go telling everyone.

00:21:28.740 --> 00:21:30.300
<i>Level 5...</i>

00:21:30.930 --> 00:21:34.820
<i>But if I stop him, the Xenos 
will go back to normal!</i>

00:21:36.740 --> 00:21:37.750
<i>Wait for me...</i>

00:21:38.740 --> 00:21:39.830
<i>Wiene!</i>

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:40.940
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:40.940
<b>Dix Perdix
The Dreams of Beasts</b>

00:23:37.380 --> 00:23:38.490
Next time,

00:23:38.490 --> 00:23:40.210
"Dix Perdix."
